    "media:imagetext": "L S\nApril 5, 1945\nES\nRECHIVED\nH. M. BIXBY\nAPR 9 1945\nOFJ\nJHS\nPMS\nERSONAT\nDear 3111:\nDuring a telephone conversation on another\nmubject yesterday evening, Ir. Bixby mentioned thet he\nend Mre. Birby appreciate very much all that you have\nascist Catherine with her living arrengenents\nin Honolulu.\nI know it de reessuring to Mr. and Mrs.\nBixby that you end Mary have token such a personal and\nhelpful interest in Catherine's living problems, parti-\nenlarly during the initial period of her Honolulu resi-\ndence when so many questions doubtleesly blagued her.\nFlense let me add my word of thanks to both\nof you for what it may be worth.\nSincerely,\nOriginal Signed by\nL. C. REYNOLDS\nI. C. Reynolde\nMr. T. J. Mullehey\nSection Superintendent\nHono lulu, I.H.\nR: 79\nbec: Vice President Bixby, NYK\nPlos",
